                <pb facs="0103" n="15" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg15"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Neutrality proclamation of the Austrian Government,
                        published in the official Wiener Zeitung on the 11th of February,
                    1904.</hi></head>
                <p>The Imperial Russian and the Imperial Japanese Governments having officially
                    informed the I. and R. ministry of foreign affairs that a state of war now
                    exists between these two powers, the Austro-Hungarian Monarchy has declared its
                    neutrality to both belligerents and will observe an attitude strictly in
                    conformity with the law of nations.</p>
                <p>It is therefore the duty of all Austrian subjects to carefully refrain from any
                    actions which might be inconsistent with the neutrality of the monarchy.</p>
            </div>
